Task 1 (evolve): fix the false "claimed success, 0 task commits" warning in the trajectory report.
• I checked git: each session directory is stamped with the session's end time. The 10:30 session's wrap-up commit is at 11:09:22Z, exactly its stamp. Its task commits (10:43 and 11:04) exist, and the check still flagged it.
• I did not read classify_session_claims in scripts/extract_trajectory.py, where the claim check lives. So "the check treats the stamp as the window start" is still a guess. The task's first step is to confirm it. If the window is already built correctly, the task records that null finding instead of inventing a change.
• The task also asks for fixture tests, a positive control (break the fix on purpose, watch it fail, restore it), and before/after counts written into ARCHITECTURE.md.

Task 2 (product): one test covering every way `--print` can write to stdout.
• --print output has had five separate fixes in two days, each with a test for its own case.
• This task adds a single test that runs yoyo --print in a temp directory against a local stub. The stub's reply includes leading blank lines, a thinking block, a tool call and the final answer.
• It asserts that stdout is exactly the answer, and that with --output-format json stdout is exactly one JSON object. It includes a positive control. If the test finds a real leak, the fix stays in src/prompt.rs.

